    PlatformOverview
        Type: Section
        Role: Content
        Caption: AIS Platform Overview
        Purpose: Summary of the three main sections of AIS Platform

        PillarEcosystem
            Type: Section
            Role: Content
            Caption: STF Semantic Ecosystem for AI Agents
            Content: Open-source specifications and self-hosting compiler infrastructure built for deterministic machine comprehension rather than human visual heuristics.
            Navigate: /ecosystem/sil/

        PillarMonitoring
            Type: Section
            Role: Content
            Caption: Sir Revizor Continuous Code Security Monitoring
            Content: Daily repository monitoring across your entire language stack. Every reported vulnerability is confirmed by actual execution with a reproducible Proof-of-Concept trace (with Solidity and Rust/WASM sample reports and an anonymized Case #NNN Coordinated Disclosure board at github.com/ais-space/disclosures), and false-positive static alerts refuted by execution are documented transparently.
            Navigate: /monitoring/sil/

        PillarCareers
            Type: Section
            Role: Content
            Caption: Independent Sales Partners & Business Co-Founder Track
            Content: B2B cybersecurity sales partners earn 20% recurring revenue share under a written agreement for as long as they service the client account, equipped with pre-qualified public open-source repositories where defects were verified locally under coordinated disclosure rules. Top performers proven in real client work are considered for Business Co-Founder.
            Navigate: /careers/sil/

    EcosystemSummary
        Type: Section
        Role: Content
        Caption: The 5 Components of the STF Ecosystem
        Purpose: Brief cards for all 5 open-source STF ecosystem projects

        CardSTF
            Type: Section
            Role: Content
            Caption: STF — Semantic Text Format
            Content: Core structural format with an explicit section tree and grammar-level trust zones (System, UserContent). Because the format is strictly machine-readable and trivially parsed, deterministic host code filters and strips unauthorized branches before they reach the agent, providing real code-enforced protection against prompt injection alongside lower inference overhead for smaller models.
            Navigate: /ecosystem/stf/sil/

        CardSIL
            Type: Section
            Role: Content
            Caption: SIL — Semantic Interface Layer
            Content: Application extension of STF for AI agent web navigation without parsing raw HTML/DOM or executing JavaScript, featuring 5 conformance profiles.
            Navigate: /ecosystem/sil-spec/sil/

        CardSTFMemory
            Type: Section
            Role: Content
            Caption: STF-Memory — Structured Agent Memory
            Content: Long-term structural memory model for agents with explicit conflict tracking, trust provenance, and projections instead of flat logs, preventing memory degradation across long multi-agent runs.
            Navigate: /ecosystem/stf-memory/sil/

        CardSIR
            Type: Section
            Role: Content
            Caption: SIR — Semantic Intermediate Representation
            Content: Executable semantic intermediate representation built on STF for AI coding agents and verifiable translation to WebAssembly.
            Navigate: /ecosystem/sir/sil/

        CardSIRCompiler
            Type: Section
            Role: Content
            Caption: SIR Compiler — Self-Hosting SIR-to-WASM Compiler
            Content: Self-compiling compiler written in SIR itself (~103 KB binary, proven byte-for-byte self-compilation fixpoint, 253/253 tests passing).
            Navigate: /ecosystem/sir-compiler/sil/

